<title>USA: Alpha acquires assets of private company.</title>
<headline>Alpha acquires assets of private company.</headline>
<dateline>SANTA ANA, Calif. 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alpha Microsystems said Tuesday that it acquired for cash the assets of privately-held Irvine, Calif.-based Data Enhancement International Inc.</p>
<p>Terms of the deal were not disclosed.</p>
<p>The company said it expects initial revenue from this acquisition to be about $1 million during the next 12 months.</p>
<p>DEI specializes in client/server development, along with local and wide area Internet and intranet networking technologies.</p>
</text>
